s inside the value; that's fine because JSON allows escaped newlines \\n. Actually the string value must contain escape sequences for newlines, not literal newlines. So we must use \\n in the string. In the JSON representation, we can either put the actual newline inside the string (which is allowed in JSON strings? Actually JSON strings cannot contain unescaped control characters, including newline. So we must escape newlines as \\n. So in the JSON produced, the newlines in the code should be represented as \\n. I'll write them as \\n in the string.\n\nSo the JSON will be:\n\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case['threshold']\\n    calls = case['calls']\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call['call_id']\\n        gain = call['loss_without_call'] - call['loss_with_call']\\n        normalized_gain = gain / call['prediction_tokens']\\n        accepted = call['parseable'] and normalized_gain >= threshold\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            'call_id': call_id,\\n            'accepted': accepted,\\n            'normalized_gain': normalized_gain\\n        })\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n    return {\\n        'accepted_call_ids': accepted_call_ids,\\n        'diagnostics': diagnostics\\n    }\"}\n\nNow we must ensure no extra whitespace. This is valid.\n\nWe'll output exactly that.\n\nBut note: The code should also include validation. I'll add a simple validation.\n\nI'll modify code to check for required fields and raise ValueError if missing.\n\nBetter:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    if not isinstance(case, dict) or 'threshold' not in case or 'calls' not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"case missing required fields\")\n    threshold = case['threshold']\n    calls = case['calls']\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"calls must be list\")\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    diagnostics = []\n    for call in calls:\n        if not isinstance(call, dict):\n            raise ValueError(\"call must be dict\")\n        for key in ('call_id', 'loss_without_call', 'loss_with_call', 'prediction_tokens', 'parseable'):\n            if key not in call:\n                raise ValueError(f\"call missing {key}\")\n        call_id = call['call_id']\n        gain = call['loss_without_call'] - call['loss_with_call']\n        tokens = call['prediction_tokens']\n        if tokens <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"prediction_tokens must be positive\")\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\n        accepted = call['parseable'] and normalized_gain >= threshold\n        diagnostics.append({\n            'call_id': call_id,\n            'accepted': accepted,\n            'normalized_gain': normalized_gain\n        })\n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    return {\n        'accepted_call_ids': accepted_call_ids,\n        'diagnostics': diagnostics\n    }\n\nThat's good. Now produce the escaped JSON.\n\nI'll write it with proper escaping. I'll also ensure no trailing spaces.\n\nLet's produce final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2164,"completion_tokens":2950,"total_tokens":5114,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2048},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2599},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2048,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":116},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}